{"title":"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A two-digit positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> has the property that when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/4/af4c37ff1a89a2667cb70c3e6e731b7040a36bfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$109$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, the remainder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. What is the sum of all such two-digit positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/d/8bdb25d6dd1f3e0d11fb1fb419265d6a339a7420.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 36  \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 56  \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 50  \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 71  \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 35  \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"430\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/c/93c3e302452ca010480ae1b4d5f33ba257b15bb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\ge 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/e/a7ed1f8b8d6ebe8643bf84affb0b70d3aeef0228.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[109 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{x} \\implies 105 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{x}.\\]\" width=\"340\" height=\"18\" />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be a two-digit factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/6/b96897bc72456752758bdf0be0f345acec5b6785.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$105 = 3\\cdot5\\cdot7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"14\" />. We can see that multiplying only one prime factor would make the factor be one-digit, while multiplying all three prime factors would make the factor be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791f15f656db201fa9116a2f762a4b292fc50883.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$105$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, the possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/b/58bb880f682cee2b5a553a128d7640216692840e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\cdot 5 = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/3/1d3506406214d8764f42d220780886a4af5f7072.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\cdot 7 = 35$\" width=\"73\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/e/a0ef13a364763004cb8318838aa5687d0f97fb02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\cdot 7 = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" />, so the sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/2/de2534def5c146098c3bcc1db9b8066cf8cb15e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 + 35 + 21 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 71}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"190\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley\">2013 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a 